Subject: [PATCH 04/24] Modeling Algorithms - Fix fillet corners on the seam of
 a periodic face

PerformOneCorner extends the edge Arcprol across the opposite face Fop.
When Arcprol lies on the seam and Fop uses it only once (a thread cut
along a cylinder, FreeCAD issue 32486), the pcurve was taken from the
side of the period that is not in Fop. Take the pcurve of the occurrence
in Fop.

The intersection curve built there may start or end on the seam, or run
along it. A point at an end of the curve no longer splits it (this threw
in Geom_TrimmedCurve), and a parallel extrema result, which has no
points, is no longer read (this crashed).

With the OnSame state, the curve of the fillet on the opposite face is
intersected with the extended face at the end. When the fillet stops on
the seam and the seam lies in that face, the crossing is the end point of
the curve. It was found slightly outside the range and rejected, and the
corner failed. A crossing within the curve resolution of the range is now
accepted and clamped.

The fillet of the thread rim is built for all radii from 0.3 to 2 mm.
Test bugs/modalg_8/fillet_thread_on_seam needs data file
freecad32486_thread.brep.

